    "abstract": "[Paraphrase] BitNet Distillation (BitDistill) is a lightweight pipeline that fine-tunes off-the-shelf full-precision LLMs such as Qwen into 1.58-bit (ternary) models for specific downstream tasks. It combines SubLN normalization, multi-head attention distillation, and continual pre-training as a warm-up. Results are comparable to the full-precision counterparts across model sizes, with up to 10x memory savings and 2.65x faster CPU inference."
