    "abstract": "[Paraphrase] PhoenixRepair is a multi-agent framework for LLM-based issue resolution. It argues that existing agents explore repair strategies too narrowly, both across candidate edit locations and across attempts at each location. It samples multiple locations, optionally adds graph-based localization for hard tasks, and iteratively reflects on and refines patches before a final round informed by all earlier attempts. On SWE-bench Verified it reports a 7.8% relative gain over SWE-agent with DeepSeek-V3.1 and 76.0% Pass@1 with MiniMax-M2.5."
